1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:07,000
Agent Spend Firewall: a safety layer between AI agents and Razorpay money.

2
00:00:07,000 --> 00:00:12,500
AI agents can now issue refunds and payouts through Razorpay's MCP tools.

3
00:00:12,500 --> 00:00:18,000
Prompt injection, retry loops or a paise/rupee mix-up can lose real money.

4
00:00:18,000 --> 00:00:23,500
Our firewall is a drop-in MCP proxy. The agent connects to it instead of Razorpay.

5
00:00:23,500 --> 00:00:29,000
Reads pass straight through. Money tools need a reason, pass policy, and get audited.

6
00:00:29,000 --> 00:00:38,000
Limits live in TypeScript policy-as-code. Anything not explicitly allowed is denied.

7
00:00:38,000 --> 00:00:45,000
Live run: a refund with no reason is rejected before it ever reaches Razorpay.

8
00:00:45,000 --> 00:00:52,000
A legitimate ₹499 refund with a clear reason is allowed and forwarded.

9
00:00:52,000 --> 00:00:59,000
The agent retries the same refund. The firewall blocks the duplicate.

10
00:00:59,000 --> 00:01:06,000
A prompt injection asks for ₹50,000. The hard cap denies it; the reason grants nothing.

11
00:01:06,000 --> 00:01:13,000
Refunding more than what's left on the payment is denied using a live payment lookup.

12
00:01:13,000 --> 00:01:19,000
₹4,500 is over the auto-approve limit, so the call is held: NOT executed.

13
00:01:19,000 --> 00:01:23,500
The approver gets a Telegram card with the amount, rule and the agent's reason.

14
00:01:23,500 --> 00:01:29,000
One tap on Approve: the firewall executes it exactly once and the agent sees the result.

15
00:01:29,000 --> 00:01:37,000
Ops flips the kill switch: every money action is frozen; read tools still work.

16
00:01:37,000 --> 00:01:43,000
Every attempt, approval and outcome is written to a hash-chained audit log.

17
00:01:43,000 --> 00:01:49,000
Edit a single row and audit:verify points to exactly where the chain broke.

18
00:01:49,000 --> 00:01:55,000
Of 7 refund attempts, only the 2 safe ones reached Razorpay. 1,939 tests pass.

19
00:01:55,000 --> 00:02:01,000
Built so far: proxy, policy, approvals, kill switch, audit. Next: dashboard and evals.
